  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Usage",
      "text": "`SimpleGrid` is a responsive grid system with equal-width columns.\nIt uses CSS grid layout. If you need to set different widths for columns, use\n[Grid](/core/grid) component instead.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "spacing and verticalSpacing props",
      "text": "`spacing` prop is used both for horizontal and vertical spacing if `verticalSpacing` is not set:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Responsive props",
      "text": "`cols`, `spacing` and `verticalSpacing` props support object notation for responsive values,\nit works the same way as [style props](/styles/style-props): the object may have `base`, `xs`,\n`sm`, `md`, `lg` and `xl` key, and values from those keys will be applied according to current\nviewport width.\n\nIn the following example, `cols={{ base: 1, sm: 2, lg: 5 }}` means:\n\n- 1 column if viewport width is less than `sm` breakpoint\n- 2 columns if viewport width is between `sm` and `lg` breakpoints\n- 5 columns if viewport width is greater than `lg` breakpoint\n\nSame logic applies to `spacing` and `verticalSpacing` props.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Container queries",
      "text": "To use [container queries](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_containment/Container_queries)\ninstead of media queries, set `type=\"container\"`. With container queries, grid columns and spacing\nwill be adjusted based on the container width, not the viewport width.\n\nNote that, when using container queries, `cols`, `spacing` and `verticalSpacing` props cannot\nreference `theme.breakpoints` values in keys. It is required to use exact px or em values.\n\nTo see how the grid changes, resize the root element of the demo\nwith the resize handle located at the bottom right corner of the demo:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Browser support",
      "text": "`SimpleGrid` uses [CSS Grid Layout](https://caniuse.com/css-grid), it is supported in all modern browsers.\nIf you need to support older browsers, use [Grid](/core/grid) (flexbox based) component instead.\n\nWhen `type=\"container\"` is set, `SimpleGrid` uses [container queries](https://caniuse.com/css-container-queries).\nSince February 2023, container queries are supported in all modern browsers. If you need to support older browsers,\ndo not use container queries option.",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
